JavaScript
Complete Learning Roadmap
From zero to mastery  -  Check off each topic as you complete it
BEGINNER	INTERMEDIATE	ADVANCED
 
Tip: Work through each phase in order. Do not rush to frameworks. Understanding the fundamentals will make everything else easier and faster to learn. Estimated times assume one to two focused hours per day.
 
Phase 1  -  The Foundations
Start here without exception. These concepts appear in every single JavaScript program ever written.
Done	Topic	Difficulty	Est. Time
[ ]	Variables and Data Types
var, let, const — numbers, strings, booleans, null, undefined, symbols	Beginner	1 - 2 days
[ ]	Operators and Expressions
Arithmetic, comparison, logical, assignment, and ternary operators	Beginner	1 day
[ ]	Control Flow
if / else, switch statements, for loops, while loops, break and continue	Beginner	2 - 3 days
[ ]	Functions
Declarations, expressions, arrow functions, parameters, default values, return	Beginner	2 - 3 days
[ ]	Scope and Hoisting
Global vs local scope, block scope, how JS hoists variables and functions	Beginner	2 days
[ ]	Arrays
Creating, accessing, iterating — map, filter, reduce, find, forEach	Beginner	3 - 4 days
[ ]	Objects
Key-value pairs, dot vs bracket notation, methods, nested objects	Beginner	3 - 4 days
[ ]	String Methods
Slice, split, join, trim, includes, template literals, string interpolation	Beginner	1 - 2 days
[ ]	Error Handling
try / catch / finally, throwing errors, built-in Error types	Beginner	1 - 2 days
 
Phase 2  -  Core JavaScript
This is where real developers are made. Master this before touching any framework.
Done	Topic	Difficulty	Est. Time
[ ]	The DOM
Selecting elements, traversing the tree, innerHTML, event listeners	Beginner	4 - 5 days
[ ]	DOM Manipulation
createElement, appendChild, removeChild, classList, setting attributes	Beginner	3 - 4 days
[ ]	Closures
Lexical scope, function factories, the classic counter example explained	Intermediate	3 - 4 days
[ ]	Higher-Order Functions
Functions that accept or return other functions, callbacks explained deeply	Intermediate	2 - 3 days
[ ]	Prototypes and Inheritance
Prototype chain, Object.create(), how JS inheritance actually works under the hood	Intermediate	3 - 4 days
[ ]	ES6 Classes
class syntax, constructor, extends, super keyword, static methods	Intermediate	2 - 3 days
[ ]	Destructuring
Array and object destructuring, default values, renaming variables	Intermediate	1 - 2 days
[ ]	Spread and Rest Operators
The ... operator for copying arrays, merging objects, variadic functions	Intermediate	1 day
[ ]	Modules (ESM)
import and export, named vs default exports, how module bundlers work	Intermediate	2 days
[ ]	The this Keyword
Implicit, explicit, new binding rules — why this changes and how arrow functions fix it	Intermediate	3 - 4 days
[ ]	Regular Expressions
Patterns, flags, test / match / replace, real-world use cases	Intermediate	3 - 4 days
 
Phase 3  -  Asynchronous JavaScript  (Most Important Phase)
Surveys consistently rank async concepts as the hardest topic for JS developers — and the most critical to understand. Take your time here.
Done	Topic	Difficulty	Est. Time
[ ]	The Event Loop
Call stack, heap, message queue — understanding how JS is single-threaded	Intermediate	2 - 3 days
[ ]	Callbacks
Async operations via callbacks, understanding callback hell and why it exists	Intermediate	2 days
[ ]	Promises
Creating promises, .then() / .catch() / .finally(), promise chaining	Intermediate	3 - 4 days
[ ]	async and await
Writing async code that reads like synchronous code, error handling patterns	Intermediate	3 - 4 days
[ ]	Fetch API
Making HTTP requests from the browser, reading JSON responses, handling errors	Intermediate	2 - 3 days
[ ]	Async Error Handling
try / catch with await, Promise.allSettled, graceful failure patterns	Intermediate	2 days
[ ]	Promise.all, race, any
Running parallel async operations, racing promises, first-success patterns	Advanced	2 days
[ ]	Web Workers
Offloading CPU-intensive tasks, postMessage communication, shared workers	Advanced	2 - 3 days
 
Phase 4  -  Browser and Web APIs
These powerful APIs are built into the browser — no installation required. They are what make JavaScript unique.
Done	Topic	Difficulty	Est. Time
[ ]	localStorage and sessionStorage
Persisting data on the client, JSON serialization, storage limits	Beginner	1 day
[ ]	Cookies
Setting, reading, expiry dates, security flags like HttpOnly and Secure	Intermediate	1 - 2 days
[ ]	Geolocation API
Getting user coordinates, handling permissions, accuracy options	Beginner	1 day
[ ]	Canvas API
Drawing 2D graphics programmatically, animations, pixel-level manipulation	Intermediate	3 - 5 days
[ ]	Intersection Observer
Lazy loading images, infinite scroll, detecting when elements enter the viewport	Intermediate	1 - 2 days
[ ]	Web Sockets
Real-time two-way communication between client and server	Advanced	3 - 4 days
[ ]	Service Workers
Background sync, offline caching strategies, foundation of Progressive Web Apps	Advanced	4 - 5 days
[ ]	WebRTC
Peer-to-peer audio and video streaming, data channels	Advanced	5 - 7 days
 
Phase 5  -  Node.js and Backend Development
Take JavaScript to the server. Node.js powers companies including Netflix, LinkedIn, PayPal, and NASA.
Done	Topic	Difficulty	Est. Time
[ ]	Node.js Fundamentals
How Node works, the global object, process, __dirname, CommonJS modules	Intermediate	3 - 4 days
[ ]	npm and package.json
Installing packages, writing scripts, version ranges, devDependencies	Beginner	1 - 2 days
[ ]	File System Module
Reading and writing files, synchronous vs asynchronous, streams	Intermediate	2 - 3 days
[ ]	HTTP Module
Creating a basic server without any framework, understanding req and res	Intermediate	2 - 3 days
[ ]	Express.js
Routing, middleware, building REST APIs, error handling middleware	Intermediate	5 - 7 days
[ ]	Environment Variables
Using .env files, the dotenv package, never hardcoding secrets	Beginner	1 day
[ ]	SQL Databases
Connecting to PostgreSQL or MySQL, writing queries, using ORMs like Prisma	Intermediate	5 - 7 days
[ ]	MongoDB and Mongoose
NoSQL document databases, schemas, CRUD operations	Intermediate	4 - 5 days
[ ]	Authentication
JSON Web Tokens, sessions, password hashing with bcrypt, OAuth basics	Advanced	5 - 7 days
[ ]	REST API Design
HTTP methods, status codes, resource naming conventions, API versioning	Intermediate	3 - 4 days
 
Phase 6  -  Modern Tooling and Ecosystem
The tools every professional JavaScript developer uses on a daily basis.
Done	Topic	Difficulty	Est. Time
[ ]	Git and GitHub
Commits, branches, merging, pull request workflow, resolving conflicts	Beginner	3 - 4 days
[ ]	TypeScript Basics
Static types, interfaces, generics, compiling to JS — why it matters for teams	Intermediate	5 - 7 days
[ ]	ESLint
Linting rules, shareable configs, auto-fix, integrating with your editor	Beginner	1 day
[ ]	Prettier
Code formatting, configuration file, working alongside ESLint	Beginner	1 day
[ ]	Vite and Webpack
How bundlers work, development server, production builds, hot module replacement	Intermediate	3 - 4 days
[ ]	Jest — Unit Testing
Writing unit tests, matchers, mocking functions and modules, code coverage	Intermediate	4 - 5 days
[ ]	Playwright or Cypress
End-to-end browser testing, selectors, running tests in CI pipelines	Advanced	4 - 5 days
[ ]	GitHub Actions
Automated testing on push, deployment pipelines, CI/CD fundamentals	Intermediate	3 - 4 days
[ ]	Docker Basics
Containerising a Node.js app, writing a Dockerfile, docker-compose	Advanced	4 - 5 days
 
Phase 7  -  Frameworks (Pick One and Go Deep)
Do not start here before completing Phases 1 to 3. React is the most in-demand framework as of the 2024 StackOverflow survey at 40.6 percent developer usage.
Done	Topic	Difficulty	Est. Time
[ ]	React — Components and JSX
Functional components, JSX syntax, rendering lists, keys, props	Intermediate	3 - 4 days
[ ]	React — Hooks
useState, useEffect, useRef, useContext, writing your own custom hooks	Intermediate	5 - 7 days
[ ]	React — State Management
Context API, Redux Toolkit, or Zustand — managing app-wide state	Advanced	5 - 7 days
[ ]	React — Routing
React Router v6, dynamic route params, protected routes, nested routes	Intermediate	2 - 3 days
[ ]	Next.js
SSR, SSG, ISR, the App Router, API routes, deployment to Vercel	Advanced	7 - 10 days
[ ]	Vue.js (alternative)
Options API vs Composition API, the Vue reactivity system, Pinia	Intermediate	7 - 10 days
[ ]	Svelte (alternative)
Compiled approach to reactivity, no virtual DOM, SvelteKit	Intermediate	5 - 7 days
 
Phase 8  -  Advanced and Mastery Topics
Senior-level concepts. Return to this phase after solid hands-on experience with Phases 1 through 7.
Done	Topic	Difficulty	Est. Time
[ ]	Design Patterns
Module, Singleton, Observer, Factory, MVC — what they are and when to use them	Advanced	7 - 10 days
[ ]	Data Structures in JS
Linked lists, stacks, queues, binary trees, hash maps — built from scratch in JS	Advanced	7 - 14 days
[ ]	Algorithms and Big O
Sorting, searching, time and space complexity — essential for technical interviews	Advanced	14+ days
[ ]	Memory Management
Garbage collection, memory leaks, WeakMap, WeakSet, WeakRef	Advanced	3 - 4 days
[ ]	Performance Optimization
Debounce, throttle, memoization, understanding virtual DOM diffing	Advanced	4 - 5 days
[ ]	Web Security (OWASP)
XSS, CSRF, SQL injection, input sanitisation, HTTPS, content security policy	Advanced	5 - 7 days
[ ]	WebAssembly
Compiling C or Rust to WASM, calling it from JS, real performance use cases	Advanced	5 - 7 days
[ ]	GraphQL
Queries, mutations, subscriptions, Apollo Client, comparing to REST	Advanced	5 - 7 days
[ ]	Microservices with Node
Service architecture, message queues with RabbitMQ or Kafka basics	Advanced	7 - 10 days
 
